186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274728 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274728 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186273906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274728 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3579701a-9198-5e56-82f7-d569880f78f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274955 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b8437634-a0b8-5fc4-8ac1-18de47b710d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275381 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275381 #edb/ref 1069 "q-157224" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275381 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275381 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275381 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97d72a17-2281-52f3-a3f9-d658f3c735d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275381 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =-2[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6-2+0 \\\\ 0+4+0 \\\\ 2-2+15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275383 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275383 #edb/ref 1069 "q-157228" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275383 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275383 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275383 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40a86374-09c1-5fcd-a58c-a5f678fb3c1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275383 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3} & =-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+0+15 \\\\ -7-10+20 \\\\ 0+0+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275384 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275384 #edb/ref 1069 "q-157236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275384 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275384 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275384 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2473ef72-1c36-57f9-bdd5-12c0b04c9229" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275384 #edb/ref 1074 "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-3+4 \\\\ 5-6+1 \\\\ 2-12+10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315249 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315249 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315249 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "172bfc45-43c6-5f9b-90f6-930b6748c07e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315321 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315321 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315321 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "24069f64-c580-5200-b5e0-1c7ef2ae7e68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315397 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315397 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315397 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30e01cba-42d8-51c3-9004-5c057629e1db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315451 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315451 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315451 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a15928d-e29a-514a-aa9c-b81e928ccc22" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
